[Music]  i want them to stick to their mission  statement about inclusion and equity and  in being there for the athletes we're  trying to grow a sport be inclusive and  you're telling me that  i  i'm literally being excluded because of  my disability i grew up in baton rouge  louisiana as a competitive gymnast and  my gymnastics career ended when i was  diagnosed with osteosarcoma bone cancer  and i had two options it was either let  cancer get the best of my life or move  on and find something that made me happy  i chose snowboarding because it reminded  me of a balance beam and if i could have  any piece of my old life back  i would have done anything to do it i do  not have a knee or a foot  not having a knee is massive in  snowboarding i competed in the 2018  paralympic games where i won two gold  medals so paralympic snowboarding is set  up in two different leg impairment  groups so you have ll1 which is the most  impaired leg disability group and then  you have ll2 which is the less impaired  disability group i currently compete in  ll1 and i competed in l01 at the korea  games  and back in 2019  the international paralympic committee  made the decision to not include  ll-1 women in the paralympics however  we were told that we could compete  in the ll2 group with the less disabled  athletes  even though we would be at a  disadvantage we were still offered that  opportunity to compete and in february  of 2021  the qualification guides came out we  were completely excluded from the  qualification guide and the program in  china  so they eliminated our category of  competition because we didn't have  enough participants i mean immediately  when we found out that we could not  compete um there was actually a rule  that said if there is less than three  women in the ll1 class they can compete  with the ll2 women so the more disabled  women competed with the less impaired  women and  in our competitions both myself and my  competitor at one event one first and  second there is no language in our  rulebook that says we can compete but  there is also no language in our  rulebook that says we cannot compete i'm  very hopeful that this can happen  because the reasoning for me to not  compete  it's not big enough it doesn't make any  sense i want the opportunity to defend  my gold medals i know given that  opportunity i can do it and i'm not  going to stop fighting  you

